@format 1
@id media-removal.common.files-actions
@title Files removal commands
@section Media removal
@area Common
@entry remove-selected, clear-files
@summary Trace direct Files commands that remove selected unlocked entries or request removal of all unlocked entries.
@related media-removal.common.docket-removal, media-removal.common.files-clear
@tag media
@tag removal
@tag common
@tag files

@alias list = Cadroue.UIShell.PPanels.PList
@alias docket = Cadroue.Application.LDocket

[remove-selected] Remove selected Files <input>
~ This starts with remove selected Files.
[Technical explanation]
- Resolve selected unlocked paths and remember the first removed index before performing synchronous docket removal @ list.PListRemove(...)
> remove-result

[clear-files] Remove all Files button <input>
~ This starts with remove all Files button.
[Technical explanation]
- Invoke the registered Remove All callback and enter PListClear @ list.PListButtonBuild(...)
> map:media-removal.common.files-clear

[remove-result] Remove eligibility <decision>
~ The program checks remove eligibility.
[Technical explanation]
- Continue only when at least one selected path is unlocked and removable @ list.PListRemove(...)
? "Removal performed" > remove-docket-call
? "Nothing removable" > remove-nochange

[remove-docket-call] Remove selected paths from docket <process>
~ This step handles remove selected paths from program file list.
[Technical explanation]
- Call LDocketPathsRemove; the common Docket removal sequence runs synchronously before PListRemove resumes @ list.PListRemove(...)
  @ docket.LDocketPathsRemove(...)
> remove-final-select

[remove-nochange] Removal ignored <output>
~ This path ends with removal ignored.
[Technical explanation]
= No program media entry is removed.

[remove-final-select] Reselect after direct removal <process>
~ This step handles reselect after direct removal.
[Technical explanation]
- Reread remaining paths and call PListSelectApply with null or the clamped original index; this publishes PListPathChange again after removal has completed @ list.PListRemove(...)
  @ list.PListSelectApply(...)
> remove-output

[remove-output] Direct Files removal completed <output>
~ This path ends with direct Files removal completed.
[Technical explanation]
= Selected unlocked entries have been offered for removal and Files selection has been reapplied to the remaining program entries.
